

# What the request is about (reason_topics/2)

An outline of the requirement, a line a subject, the subject most said about first:

- Transaction: every transaction has the snapshot; every transaction begins at the latest_version; every transaction that is active may stage the insertion; every transaction that is active may stage the deletion; every transaction that is active is may_commit; every transaction that is active is may_abort; every transaction that is active may read the key; every transaction that is active may print the view; every transaction that is not active causes the error.
- Key: every key is an integer; every key that is visible reads as "yes"; every key that is not visible reads as "no"; every key that is visible is printed; every key that is committed gets "yes"; every key that is not committed gets "no"; every key has the staged_change.
- Commit: every commit is atomic; every commit applies the changes to the latest_version; every commit creates the version; every commit increments the commit_id; every commit ends the transaction; every commit that is empty increments the commit_id; every commit that follows the snapshot is invisible.
- Mvccs, a program: simulates the tree; reads the line; does not print the prompt; does not print the debug_output.
- B_tree: a tree; a committed_version; every b_tree holds the keys.
- Ignored: a line that is blank; a redundant_insertion; a redundant_deletion.
- Neg: a view that is empty; an absent_key; an unfinished_transaction.
- View: every view that is empty does not print the line; every view is a snapshot; every view holds the changes.
- Unfinished_transaction: every unfinished_transaction is active; every unfinished_transaction is abandoned; every unfinished_transaction is not committed.
- The tree: Mvccs simulates it.
- The line: Mvccs reads it.
- Line: every line holds the command; every line that is blank is ignored.
- Repeated_begin: every repeated_begin begins the active_transaction; every repeated_begin causes the error.
- Abort: every abort discards the changes; every abort ends the transaction.
- Blind_deletion: every blind_deletion deletes the invisible_key; every blind_deletion is staged.
- Redundant_insertion: every redundant_insertion inserts the present_key; every redundant_insertion is ignored.
- Redundant_deletion: every redundant_deletion deletes the absent_key; every redundant_deletion is ignored.
- Recursive: an insertion; a deletion.
- Unbounded: a key_count; a transaction_count.
- Program (Mvccs).
- Tree: every tree is a b_tree.
- The minimum_degree: 2.
- Integer: a key.
- Negative_integer: every negative_integer may be the key.
- May_commit: a transaction that is active.
- May_abort: a transaction that is active.
- Atomic: a commit.
- Printed: a key that is visible.
- Ascending: a printing.
- Printing: every printing is ascending.
- Version_command: every version_command prints the commit_id.
- Word: a transaction_name.
- Transaction_name: every transaction_name is a word.
- Snapshot: a view.
- Invisible: a commit that follows the snapshot.
- Kept: a change that is last.
- Change: every change that is last is kept.
- Staged: a blind_deletion.
- Win: a committer that is last.
- Committer: every committer that is last is win.
- Committed_key: a present_key.
- Present_key: every present_key is a committed_key.
- Absent_key: every absent_key is not a committed_key.
- Active: an unfinished_transaction.
- Abandoned: an unfinished_transaction.
- Committed_version: every committed_version is a b_tree.
- Insertion: every insertion is recursive.
- Deletion: every deletion is recursive.
- Heap_allocated: a node.
- Node: every node is heap_allocated.
- Key_count: every key_count is unbounded.
- Transaction_count: every transaction_count is unbounded.
- Command: every command prints the answer.